# CasperOS — apt pinning for trixie-backports.
#
# Priority 100 = "only if explicitly asked for" (or already installed). Without
# this, adding the backports suite would let apt pull newer libc, systemd and
# i915-era userspace into a stable image on the next `apt upgrade`.
#
# Nothing in the image needs backports any more: the GNOME desktop comes from
# trixie itself. The pin stays so that a backports entry appearing in a source
# list can never silently upgrade the base system, and so anyone who enables
# trixie-backports later (for a newer kernel, say) gets the safe behaviour.
Package: *
Pin: release n=trixie-backports
Pin-Priority: 100
